      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/ns#Process",
      "name": "Remote-mount a dependency",
      "summary": "Laying a harness — and every instance it needs — down from another repository at a pinned commit, as declared directories, with a lock that says exactly what arrived.",
      "description": "Laying a harness — and every instance it needs — down from another repository at a pinned commit, as declared directories, with a lock that says exactly what arrived.\n\nYou are in this process whenever a folio or harness needs a layer it does not hold: a downstream folio built on a content layer above this harness, a separated instance whose foundation lives elsewhere. The downstream names the harness, its repository and a 40-character pin as a `source.remote` instance in its root `index.config.json` (legacy: `remoteMounts` on its declaration, never both); everything else is read from the harness's own declaration at that pin.\n\nEvery instance reached ends in one of three states — mounted, missing, could-not-determine — and the third is never reported as the first. The skill is `remote-mount`.",
      "enforcement": "strict",
      "sourcePath": "processes/kg/mount-dependency.bpmn",
